so how much would you pay for the  ultimate in game controller  customization would you pay a hundred  dollars what about 150 because that's  how much the xbox elite controller costs  a hundred and fifty dollars and yeah  that's a lot but the elite controller  offers more customization over anything  I've ever seen first off this thing is  dead sexy it's got a real nice way to it  more so than the existing Xbox one  controller it feels great in my hands  not to mention it's got a smooth  rubberized coating throughout and it's  just a really slick and smooth looking  controller ok so the customization  that's the focal point on the controller  the elite ships with three sets of  stainless steel analog sticks each  bearing in height and tip design you can  even mix and match each to your heart's  content there's also two types of deep  heads as well one traditional plus shape  and another octagon looking thing that  should help hitting those directional  diagonals best of all everything's  magnetic the d-pads and sticks easily  swap out with one another even the  triggers can be modified each has a  switch that lets you alternate between  full and hair trigger mode the latter of  which stops you from having to pull the  trigger all the way down then there's  the interchangeable back pedals these  are small little levers that allow you  to enter a command using just your  middle finger around back now you need  to program these with a free app for  Xbox one which lets you assign any  controller input to those back pedals  you can even remap the entire controller  to microsoft says that developer design  control schemes will be available for  the elite all accessible through that  xbox one app there's a switch on the  controller as well and that'll let you  go back and forth  between two loaded profiles not a huge  fan of those backpedals I mostly played  with them removed but some players love  them because you can bind them to car  controls or use them as a quicker way to  access something like a grenade toss or  melee I just found myself hitting them a  lot by accident so I didn't use finally  the elite controller will also work with  Windows 10 and it will even work  wirelessly if you buy a $25 adapter but  the question you've got to be asking is  is this worth 150 dollars well that  depends right the elite costs more than  twice the amount of a regular controller  and you could argue it has more than  twice the amount of features but is it  twice as better probably not not really  sure competitive players will likely  love this because of the endless amount  of customization and those twitch  controls we talked about now if that  stuff doesn't mean much to you then the  elite shouldn't be your go-to controller  but for $150 you are getting a  top-of-the-line fully customizable and  gorgeous controller that can work on PC  and Xbox one
 

